lts."}, "teachingTool": {"kind": "case-board", "version": 1, "frames": [{"title": "G · Fluid machine — side view and connections", "image": "/trades-etf/fluid.svg", "alt": "G · Fluid machine — side view and connections. Trace G from input to output and compare it with the actual device before replacing parts. A disconnected route and a binding guide are different faults.", "prompt": "Trace G from input to output and compare it with the actual device before replacing parts. A disconnected route and a binding guide are different faults.", "body": "Read written dimensions; this screen drawing is not to scale. Keep the supplied plan beside your physical work."}]}}, {"id": "mvp-etf-3-09-plan-example", "type": "worked_example", "prompt": "Convert units before comparing readings.", "equation": "2.4 cm = 24 mm; 24 − 20 = 4 mm above a 20-mm target.", "work": "Subtracting 2.4 from 20 without converting units gives a meaningless comparison.", "answer": "Apply the method to your own dimensions or the supplied independent check."}, {"id": "mvp-etf-3-09-make", "type": "prose", "markdown": "Continue the project: build, test, and change a physical feature.", "workshop": {"pageBreakBefore": true, "stage": "Make", "title": "Make the project", "lead": "Continue the project: build, test, and change a physical feature.", "minutes": 45, "notebook": "Record the changed part while you build; retain the earlier version or sketch.", "steps": ["Teacher selects a clinic using the evidence: unit conversion, ratio, repeatability or assembly interpretation.", "Diagnose a teacher-selected low-risk fault such as a loose mount; explain before making the repair.", "Repair, cycle and inspect the real device; do a fresh individual check."], "purpose": "Trades math • measuring and inspection • drawing/plan interpretation", "catchUp": ["Use a larger drawing, fraction strip or teacher-modeled example, then do a fresh measurement and calculation yourself.", "If absent or equipment is unavailable, complete 